; claude: the ray tracer, the other renderer (plan_raytracing_teaching.md,
; notes_raytracing.md): for each pixel, what does the eye see through
; it? One idea per module, as graphics/3d's rasterizer, which it is the
; counterpart of. Pure OCaml over geometry/ (Vec3, Camera, Ray,
; Material) and Rgba_image, so it runs natively and in a browser. A
; private library (see graphics/core/dune), in the elm_playground
; package: the Povray way, in the 2D playground, is its user, with the
; software 3D backend's -raytrace and "y".
(library
 (name graphics_raytrace)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
   graphics_3d_geometry ; Vec3, Camera, Ray, Material
   graphics_rgba ; Rgba_image, the picture made
 )
